  "reasoning": "The patient presents with systemic symptoms including fever, headache, weakness, and fatigue, along with swollen lymph nodes indicating an active immune response. The inability to concentrate is attributed directly to the fever, which is consistent with the high-grade fevers and chills seen in certain parasitic infections. Among the provided options, respiratory conditions like asthma, pneumonia, and the common cold typically feature prominent cough, breathing difficulties, or nasal congestion, which are absent here. Gastrointestinal issues like typhoid or GERD would emphasize abdominal pain or heartburn. Dengue usually highlights severe joint/muscle pain and retro-orbital pain. Diabetes, hypertension, psoriasis, varicose veins, cervical spondylosis, and arthritis do not align with acute febrile illness. Malaria classically presents with high fever, severe headache, profound weakness and fatigue, and can cause cognitive impairment or trouble concentrating due to the intensity of the fever and chills. Therefore, malaria is the most accurate diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]malaria[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}
